{
  "_comment": [
    "Shared test vectors for the visual-beat phase contract (T85 studio / A34 stage).",
    "beatPhase(elapsedMs, intervalMs, beats) -> { beatIndex, lit, emphasis }.",
    "T85 (web/studio, TS) authors these; A34 (app, Kotlin) implements the same function",
    "and runs the SAME vectors, so the two renderers cannot silently disagree about when a",
    "beat happens. Values are hand-derived from the definition, NOT emitted by either impl,",
    "so an off-by-one in code fails against them (red-first).",
    "Definition: beatIndex = floor(elapsed/interval); active = elapsed>=0 && beatIndex<beats;",
    "msSince = elapsed - beatIndex*interval; decay = min(220, interval*0.75);",
    "litWindow = min(decay, interval*0.3); lit = active && msSince < litWindow;",
    "emphasis = active && beatIndex % 4 == 0.",
    "The 666.666... interval (90 bpm) cases guard the app's original Long-truncation bug",
    "(60000L/90 = 666, not 666.67): at elapsed 1333 the true interval gives beat 1, a",
    "truncated 666 would give beat 2."
  ],
